gic400.library/QueryIntRoute                       gic400.library/QueryIntRoute

   NAME
	QueryIntRoute -- get the CPU targets of an interrupt

   SYNOPSIS
	mask = QueryIntRoute( irq )
	d0                    d0

	LONG QueryIntRoute(ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	Reads the target list of a shared peripheral interrupt.

   INPUTS
	irq             The SPI ID (32 or above).

   RESULTS
	mask            A bit mask, bit n set when CPU n is a target; or a
	                negative GIC400_ERR_* code (GIC400_ERR_NOT_ROUTABLE
	                for IDs below 32, GIC400_ERR_INVALID_IRQ if out of
	                range).

   NOTE
	As of V1.3 a failure returns one of the distinct negative GIC400_ERR_*
	codes, as a LONG. Prior to V1.3 every failure returned -1, whatever the
	cause, and the result was a ULONG.

   SEE ALSO
	gic400.library/RouteIntToCpu(),
	gic400.library/UnrouteIntFromCpu()

gic400.library/RemIntServerEx                     gic400.library/RemIntServerEx

   NAME
	RemIntServerEx -- remove the interrupt server of a GIC-400 interrupt

   SYNOPSIS
	error = RemIntServerEx( irq, interrupt )
	d0                      d0   a1

	LONG RemIntServerEx(ULONG, struct Interrupt *);

   FUNCTION
	Disables the interrupt, unroutes it from CPU 0 and removes the
	server installed by AddIntServerEx().

   INPUTS
	irq             The interrupt ID. SPIs start at 32; the valid range is
	                0 up to the number of IDs reported by
	                GetControllerInfo() (maxIrqs, at most 1020).
	interrupt       The structure given to AddIntServerEx() for this
	                interrupt.

   RESULTS
	error           0 on success, GIC400_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT if interrupt
	                is NULL or is not the registered server,
	                GIC400_ERR_NOT_FOUND if no server is registered,
	                GIC400_ERR_INVALID_IRQ if irq is out of range.

   NOTE
	As of V1.3 a failure returns one of the distinct negative GIC400_ERR_*
	codes, as a LONG. Prior to V1.3 every failure returned -1, whatever the
	cause, and the result was a ULONG.

   SEE ALSO
	gic400.library/AddIntServerEx()

gic400.library/RouteIntToCpu                       gic400.library/RouteIntToCpu

   NAME
	RouteIntToCpu -- add a CPU to the targets of an interrupt

   SYNOPSIS
	error = RouteIntToCpu( irq, cpu )
	d0                     d0   d1

	LONG RouteIntToCpu(ULONG, UBYTE);

   FUNCTION
	Sets the bit of a CPU in the target list of a shared peripheral
	interrupt. Other targets are kept.

   INPUTS
	irq             The SPI ID (32 or above).
	cpu             CPU index, 0 to 7.

   RESULTS
	error           0 on success, GIC400_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT if cpu is 8
	                or more, GIC400_ERR_NOT_ROUTABLE if irq is an SGI or
	                PPI (below 32), GIC400_ERR_INVALID_IRQ if irq is out
	                of range.

   NOTE
	As of V1.3 a failure returns one of the distinct negative GIC400_ERR_*
	codes, as a LONG. Prior to V1.3 every failure returned -1, whatever the
	cause, and the result was a ULONG.

   SEE ALSO
	gic400.library/UnrouteIntFromCpu(),
	gic400.library/QueryIntRoute()

