gic400.library/SetIntPriority                     gic400.library/SetIntPriority

   NAME
	SetIntPriority -- set the priority of an interrupt

   SYNOPSIS
	error = SetIntPriority( irq, priority )
	d0                      d0   d1

	LONG SetIntPriority(ULONG, UBYTE);

   FUNCTION
	Writes the priority byte of an interrupt. A lower value is a
	higher priority.

   INPUTS
	irq             The interrupt ID. SPIs start at 32; the valid range is
	                0 up to the number of IDs reported by
	                GetControllerInfo() (maxIrqs, at most 1020).
	priority        GIC priority byte. In non-secure mode the least
	                significant bit reads as 0.

   RESULTS
	error           0 on success, GIC400_ERR_INVALID_IRQ if irq is out of
	                range.

   NOTE
	As of V1.3 a failure returns one of the distinct negative GIC400_ERR_*
	codes, as a LONG. Prior to V1.3 every failure returned -1, whatever the
	cause, and the result was a ULONG.

   SEE ALSO
	gic400.library/GetIntPriority(),
	gic400.library/SetPriorityMask()

gic400.library/SetIntTriggerEdge               gic400.library/SetIntTriggerEdge

   NAME
	SetIntTriggerEdge -- configure an interrupt as edge-triggered

   SYNOPSIS
	error = SetIntTriggerEdge( irq )
	d0                         d0

	LONG SetIntTriggerEdge(ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	Programs the interrupt for edge-triggered operation.

   INPUTS
	irq             The interrupt ID. SPIs start at 32; the valid range is
	                0 up to the number of IDs reported by
	                GetControllerInfo() (maxIrqs, at most 1020).

   RESULTS
	error           0 on success, GIC400_ERR_INVALID_IRQ if irq is out of
	                range.

   NOTE
	The configuration of SGIs (IDs 0 to 15) is fixed: for those the
	call does nothing and still returns 0.

	As of V1.3 a failure returns one of the distinct negative GIC400_ERR_*
	codes, as a LONG. Prior to V1.3 every failure returned -1, whatever the
	cause, and the result was a ULONG.

   SEE ALSO
	gic400.library/SetIntTriggerLevel()

