gic400.library/SetPriorityMask                   gic400.library/SetPriorityMask

   NAME
	SetPriorityMask -- set the priority mask of the CPU interface

   SYNOPSIS
	error = SetPriorityMask( mask )
	d0                       d0

	LONG SetPriorityMask(UBYTE);

   FUNCTION
	Writes the priority mask register of the CPU interface. Only
	interrupts whose priority value is numerically lower than the
	mask are signalled to the CPU.

	The library sets the mask to 0x7F at startup.

   INPUTS
	mask            The priority mask.

   RESULTS
	error           0 on success, GIC400_ERR_NOT_READY if the library is
	                not initialised.

   NOTE
	The mask is global: it affects every interrupt of every user of
	the library.

	As of V1.3 a failure returns one of the distinct negative GIC400_ERR_*
	codes, as a LONG. Prior to V1.3 every failure returned -1, whatever the
	cause, and the result was a ULONG.

   SEE ALSO
	gic400.library/GetPriorityMask(),
	gic400.library/SetIntPriority()

gic400.library/UnrouteIntFromCpu               gic400.library/UnrouteIntFromCpu

   NAME
	UnrouteIntFromCpu -- remove a CPU from the targets of an interrupt

   SYNOPSIS
	error = UnrouteIntFromCpu( irq, cpu )
	d0                         d0   d1

	LONG UnrouteIntFromCpu(ULONG, UBYTE);

   FUNCTION
	Clears the bit of a CPU in the target list of a shared
	peripheral interrupt. Other targets are kept.

   INPUTS
	irq             The SPI ID (32 or above).
	cpu             CPU index, 0 to 7.

   RESULTS
	error           0 on success, GIC400_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT if cpu is 8
	                or more, GIC400_ERR_NOT_ROUTABLE if irq is an SGI or
	                PPI (below 32), GIC400_ERR_INVALID_IRQ if irq is out
	                of range.

   NOTE
	As of V1.3 a failure returns one of the distinct negative GIC400_ERR_*
	codes, as a LONG. Prior to V1.3 every failure returned -1, whatever the
	cause, and the result was a ULONG.

   SEE ALSO
	gic400.library/RouteIntToCpu(), gic400.library/QueryIntRoute()

